{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review the national framework governing the school year in England",
        "additional_details": "The review should consider alternative models to the typical school year, including requiring local authorities and other school employers to redistribute some summer holiday time across the academic year.\r\n \r\nThe current typical school year can create significant pressures for children and families. We want Government to assess its impact on children\u2019s wellbeing, SEND, childcare affordability, parents\u2019 ability to work and family finances, alongside educational outcomes and staff wellbeing. The same number of school days could potentially be distributed differently.",
        "background": "Review if legislation and regulations governing the number and distribution of school days and holidays remain appropriate, including the role of school employers in setting term dates. Issue guidance or legislate if changes are needed. ",
